                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ad90a7f2-180f-38e2-9d60-74fcee924814",
                        "entry_id": "98bccee3-4dc6-3718-929a-223649d27424",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A simple, distinctively American four-wheeled horse-drawn wagon designed for personal transport as well as for transporting animal fodder and domestic goods, often with a spring-mounted seat for the driver."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8b86242-00f5-4b87-b129-57294f4159cf",
                                "sense_id": "ad90a7f2-180f-38e2-9d60-74fcee924814",
                                "text": "In a few hours he would actually be at Highwater. Perhaps there would be a real buckboard at the station; perhaps the first man he saw would be some old-timer who would remember that it was McCumber who had first blazed a way through Highwater County."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57d480cf-bf90-4ff0-aa30-65176a794ae5",
                                "sense_id": "ad90a7f2-180f-38e2-9d60-74fcee924814",
                                "text": "[…] he turned to Differ and said in an employer's tone, \"Got everything ready?\"\n\"On the buckboard,\" said Differ in the tone of a Capricornian employee."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15f6ae8e-d828-4e4a-a443-0c011865b54f",
                                "sense_id": "ad90a7f2-180f-38e2-9d60-74fcee924814",
                                "text": "When he turned his head, aiming for a last look at Brother, turned it as much as the rope that connected his neck to the axle of a buckboard allowed, and, later on, when they fastened the iron around his ankles and clamped the wrists as well, there was no outward sign of trembling at all."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
